  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "The back overlaps to the end line",
  "description": "Half rink with a goalkeeper. Back A starts with the ball in the middle just inside the centre line, midfielder C stands centrally a little outside the penalty area and forward B out on the left.\n\nA passes to C and immediately skates in a curve out towards the right side. C plays a one-touch give-and-go into the space in front of A along the board. A carries the ball all the way down to the end line and plays an angled pass back. Meanwhile B has skated in towards the penalty area and finishes with a first-time shot. C follows in towards goal for any rebound.\n\nSwap roles after each attack and work on both sides. Progression: a passive and then an active defender tracking B. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The back sets off straight after the pass – the overlap has to come at full speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Play the return pass in front of A, not at A."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Play the cut-back hard along the ice and angled back, away from the goalkeeper."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "B: time your run so you are at speed when the ball arrives – not too early."
    }
  ],
